ainer"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F2.pic1.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">next profile</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 583.17 -19.42 L 583.17 -35.95 L 439.05 -35.95 L 439.05 -33.68"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 439.05 -33.68)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 477.24 -47.84)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.59em;--ltx-fo-height:0.61em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:7.97pt;" height="8.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 6.73)" width="61.69"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F2.pic1.7" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">episode reset</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></svg></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>High-level pipeline of contract-based compositional shielding.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Assume-Guarantee Contracts</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume-guarantee reasoning is a technique from the toolkit of <em id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">compositional verification</em>. In the multi-agent setting we use it to control how much coordination information each local shield may rely on. We write <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A\rangle C\langle G\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A\rangle C\langle G\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> to mean that component <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> guarantees <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> under assumption <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. A local contract can say more than “avoid a violation”: it can also encode coordination promises that make globally safe and high-return behaviour available under decentralised execution.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by defining the local action rectangles used as shield interfaces:</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Local Action Rectangle)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At an environment state <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, a local action rectangle (or simply rectangle) is a non-empty Cartesian product</p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="R\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}R^{1}\times\cdots\times R^{n}\qquad\text{with}\qquad\emptyset\neq R^{i}\subseteq d^{i}(s)\quad\text{for every }i\in\mathsf{Ag}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mtext>with</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo>≠</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mtext>for every </mtext><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖠𝗀</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}R^{1}\times\cdots\times R^{n}\qquad\text{with}\qquad\emptyset\neq R^{i}\subseteq d^{i}(s)\quad\text{for every }i\in\mathsf{Ag}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\subseteq d(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\subseteq d(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, and each factor <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the local action mask exposed to agent <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We write traces over the global alphabet as words in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>, finite prefixes as words in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, and agent-<math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> observations as their pointwise projections to <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}})^{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}})^{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math>. Next, we introduce local obligations and contracts.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Local Obligation)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A local <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math> obligation for agent <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is a formula <math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}\in\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}\in\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> over that agent’s local alphabet.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 3</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Contract)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A <math id="Thmdefinition3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math> contract is a tuple of local obligations, one for each agent,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">A contract can certify safety only when the conjunction of its local obligations entails the shared global safety objective. Together, Definitions <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Local Obligation) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Contract) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>
fix the local syntactic objects used below. Their semantics is lifted to global traces by projection: for each component, define
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\llbracket\varphi_{i}\rrbracket\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{\tau\in\mathcal{T}\mid\tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket\varphi_{i}\rrbracket\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{\tau\in\mathcal{T}\mid\tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}\},</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the pointwise projection of <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ap}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ap}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a contract <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\llbracket\mathcal{C}\rrbracket\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigcap_{i=1}^{n}\llbracket\varphi_{i}\rrbracket." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">⋂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\llbracket\mathcal{C}\rrbracket\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigcap_{i=1}^{n}\llbracket\varphi_{i}\rrbracket.</annotation></semantics></math>
Equivalently, for every global trace <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\tau\in\llbracket\mathcal{C}\rrbracket\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\},\ \tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟦</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\llbracket\mathcal{C}\rrbracket\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\forall i\in\{1,\dots,n\},\ \tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math>
This lets local obligations be interpreted on global traces by ignoring propositions outside the corresponding agent alphabet. For a global formula
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi\in\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi\in\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap})</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Psi</annotation></semantics></math> when
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\forall\tau\in\mathcal{T}.\left(\forall i\in\mathsf{Ag},\ \tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}\right)\Longrightarrow\tau\models\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖠𝗀</mi><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↾</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em">⊧</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>⊧</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\forall\tau\in\mathcal{T}.\left(\forall i\in\mathsf{Ag},\ \tau\!\upharpoonright_{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}\models\varphi_{i}\right)\Longrightarrow\tau\models\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>.
Semantic entailment involving local obligations is always understood through this lifted interpretation. Thus a contract is a decomposition of the global requirement into local promises.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 4</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Finite Contract Search Space)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix a formula-depth bound <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and, for each agent <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, a finite local formula language <math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Form}_{i}^{\leq D}\subseteq\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖥𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Form}_{i}^{\leq D}\subseteq\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}(\mathsf{Ap}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. The finite contract search space is
<math id="Thmdefinition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{Form}_{i}^{\leq D}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>𝖥𝗈𝗋𝗆</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathsf{Form}_{i}^{\leq D}.</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Circular Contract Assumptions)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a candidate contract <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, the local assume-guarantee obligation of agent <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\rangle i\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\rangle i\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle,</annotation></semantics></math>
where
<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{j\neq i}\varphi_{j}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mo>⋀</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{j\neq i}\varphi_{j}.</annotation></semantics></math>
The conjunction in <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is semantic notation using the lifted
interpretation above: it denotes the intersection
<math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcap_{j\neq i}\llbracket\varphi_{j}\rrbracket" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>⋂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">⟦</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟧</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcap_{j\neq i}\llbracket\varphi_{j}\rrbracket</annotation></semantics></math> over global traces, and may
therefore combine obligations whose syntax ranges over different local
alphabets. When the index set is empty, the conjunction is <math id="Thmdefinition5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\top" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\top</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Thus agent <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> may rely on the other agents satisfying their local obligations, while it must satisfy its own obligation. This is circular assume-guarantee reasoning: the obligations in <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> justify one another as a simultaneous contract rather than through a fixed linear order. Certification below checks the whole tuple at once: each agent may rely on the other obligations only because the fixed point proves that the projected shields preserve all obligations simultaneously, which enables sound circularity. The automata used for this certification are defined next.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Contract Safety Automata)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a contract <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, each local obligation <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is compiled into a contract safety automaton
<math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(Q_{i},q_{i}^{0},\Sigma_{i},\delta_{i},B_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(Q_{i},q_{i}^{0},\Sigma_{i},\delta_{i},B_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math>
where <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a finite set of states, <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}^{0}\in Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}^{0}\in Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the initial state, <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}:Q_{i}\times\Sigma_{i}\to Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}:Q_{i}\times\Sigma_{i}\to Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the total transition function, and <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}\subseteq Q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}\subseteq Q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is an absorbing set of bad states. Writing <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> for the finite-word extension of <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, the finite words that reach <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are exactly the bad prefixes of <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\delta_{i}^{\ast}(q_{i}^{0},w)\in B_{i}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\forall\tau_{i}\in\Sigma_{i}^{\omega}.\;w\tau_{i}\not\models\varphi_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>ω</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em">.</mo><mi>w</mi><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊧̸</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}^{\ast}(q_{i}^{0},w)\in B_{i}\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad\forall\tau_{i}\in\Sigma_{i}^{\omega}.\;w\tau_{i}\not\models\varphi_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Thus a local trace satisfies <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> precisely when no finite prefix reaches <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. For compactness, write <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}(s)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathcal{L}(s)\cap\mathsf{Ap}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}(s)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathcal{L}(s)\cap\mathsf{Ap}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for the projection of the global label at <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> to agent <math id="Thmdefinition6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s alphabet.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Contract Product)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a candidate contract <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> with contract
safety automata <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>i</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{i}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> from
Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (Contract Safety Automata) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the contract product has state space
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathcal{S}\times Q_{1}\times\cdots\times Q_{n}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathcal{S}\times Q_{1}\times\cdots\times Q_{n}.</annotation></semantics></math>
A product state is written <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,q_{1},\dots,q_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,q_{1},\dots,q_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the current automaton state for agent <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s obligation. The initial contract product state is
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(s_{0},\delta_{1}(q_{1}^{0},\ell_{1}(s_{0})),\dots,\delta_{n}(q_{n}^{0},\ell_{n}(s_{0})))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(s_{0},\delta_{1}(q_{1}^{0},\ell_{1}(s_{0})),\dots,\delta_{n}(q_{n}^{0},\ell_{n}(s_{0}))).</annotation></semantics></math>
A contract product state is locally safe if <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\notin B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\notin B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for every agent. For a legal joint action <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a=(a^{1},\dots,a^{n})\in d(s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a=(a^{1},\dots,a^{n})\in d(s)</annotation></semantics></math>, the qualitative successor set is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}},a)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\left\{(s^{\prime},\delta_{1}(q_{1},\ell_{1}(s^{\prime})),\dots,\delta_{n}(q_{n},\ell_{n}(s^{\prime})))\;\middle|\;s^{\prime}\in\Supp(\mathcal{P}(s,a))\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Post</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}},a)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\left\{(s^{\prime},\delta_{1}(q_{1},\ell_{1}(s^{\prime})),\dots,\delta_{n}(q_{n},\ell_{n}(s^{\prime})))\;\middle|\;s^{\prime}\in\Supp(\mathcal{P}(s,a))\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition7.p1.2" class="ltx_p">A contract-product execution from <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an alternating sequence
<math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m11" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\langle x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{0}x_{1}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{1}\cdots\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{0}x_{1}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{1}\cdots\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>
such that, writing <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="Thmdefinition7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in d(s_{t})\qquad\text{and}\qquad x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mtext>and</mtext><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Post</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in d(s_{t})\qquad\text{and}\qquad x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">The contract product in Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition7" title="Definition 7 (Contract Product) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> is the natural Markov state space for shielded controllers.
In decentralised learning, agent <math id="S4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> uses the active contract identifier together with an augmentation sufficient to recover its projected mask.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Contract Product Shields</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn a candidate contract into actual local shields. For a fixed <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, the shield construction computes one shared assume-guarantee fixed point over <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and then projects the resulting action relation to each agent.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 8</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Contract Predecessor)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At a contract product state <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,q_{1},\dots,q_{n})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,q_{1},\dots,q_{n})</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> range over
local action rectangles at <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math> in the sense of
Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1 (Local Action Rectangle) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
For <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W\subseteq X^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W\subseteq X^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, such a rectangle is <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>-closed at <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> if</p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}},a)\subseteq W\text{ for every }a\in R(x^{\mathcal{C}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Post</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> for every </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}},a)\subseteq W\text{ for every }a\in R(x^{\mathcal{C}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmdefinition8.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(W,x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(W,x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>-closed local action rectangles at <math id="Thmdefinition8.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The assume-guarantee predecessor operator is</p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\left\{x^{\mathcal{C}}\in X^{\mathcal{C}}\;\middle|\;\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}x^{\mathcal{C}}\text{ is locally safe and}\\
\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(W,x^{\mathcal{C}})\neq\emptyset\end{array}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.447em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext> is locally safe and</mtext></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W)\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\left\{x^{\mathcal{C}}\in X^{\mathcal{C}}\;\middle|\;\begin{array}[]{@{}l@{}}x^{\mathcal{C}}\text{ is locally safe and}\\
\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(W,x^{\mathcal{C}})\neq\emptyset\end{array}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition9" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 9</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Rectangular Winning Region)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The rectangular winning region of the contract product is the greatest fixed
point
<math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\nu W.\,\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.337em">.</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>W</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\nu W.\,\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W).</annotation></semantics></math>
It is the largest locally safe region from which the shield can offer a
non-empty Cartesian action interface closed under all induced successors. For
<math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, write
<math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}},x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}},x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>
for the winning rectangles available at <math id="Thmdefinition9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The operator <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotone. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is
finite, the descending iteration <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{0}=X^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{0}=X^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{k+1}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{k+1}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(W_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> stabilises at
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so
<math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
This fixed point is the certificate used below.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition10" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 10</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Certified Contract)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition10.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A candidate contract <math id="Thmdefinition10.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is <em id="Thmdefinition10.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">certified</em> if:</p>
<ol id="S4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the local obligations entail the global safety objective under lifted
semantics, <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the initial contract product state <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The entailment condition makes the local promises sufficient for global safety. The winning-region condition makes them operational: from the initial state, a non-empty decentralised interface can keep the active contract outside all bad states. Thus certification fails only when the promises are too weak or not enforceable by a rectangular shield from the start.
This is the initial-state condition used by Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 5.1 Library Construction: Bounded Certified Profile Search ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. For every <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose any certified rectangle <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\in\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\in\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>. This membership is the closure certificate: every joint action in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> is legal and has all contract-product successors in <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Where multiple rectangles satisfy this property, we use a deterministic tie-breaker which orders choices lexicographically maximising <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\sum_{i}|R^{i}|,\prod_{i}|R^{i}|,(R^{1},\dots,R^{n}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\sum_{i}|R^{i}|,\prod_{i}|R^{i}|,(R^{1},\dots,R^{n}))</annotation></semantics></math>, with each <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> ordered by the local action order. The safety results hold in generality, for any choice satisfying the closure certificate. The tie-breaker allows fixing a reproducible shield.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition11" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 11</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Projected Local Shield)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition11.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition11.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a certified contract <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and product state <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
deployed local shield for agent <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection
<math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}R_{\mathcal{C}}^{i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mpadded voffset="-0.2pt"><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-1.01px" height="5.95" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 4.45 5.95" width="4.45"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#5C6269;" fill="#5C6269" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,5.95) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.23,0) translate(0,3.1)"> <path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z"></path> </g> </svg> </mtext></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
