The shield is defined only on <math id="Thmdefinition11.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition12" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 12</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Local Mask Identifiability)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a certified contract <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, the projected shield is locally mask-identifiable for agent <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> if some function of the active contract identifier and agent-<math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s observation history returns <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mpadded voffset="-0.2pt"><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-1.01px" height="5.95" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 4.45 5.95" width="4.45"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#5C6269;" fill="#5C6269" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,5.95) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.23,0) translate(0,3.1)"> <path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z"></path> </g> </svg> </mtext></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> for every reachable contract-product execution and time <math id="Thmdefinition12.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition11" title="Definition 11 (Projected Local Shield) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> fixes the local mask exposed to agent <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>: the <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>th factor of a certified rectangle. Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition12" title="Definition 12 (Local Mask Identifiability) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> is the corresponding information condition for decentralised execution; it requires that this factor be computable from the active contract identifier and the information available to agent <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>
(for example, its augmented local contract-product state), without necessitating agent <math id="S4.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> to reconstruct the other agents’ masks.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition13" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 13</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Admitted Joint Actions)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition13.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a certified contract <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and product state <math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the
joint-action relation admitted by the deployed local shields is
<math id="Thmdefinition13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\prod_{i\in\mathsf{Ag}}\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖠𝗀</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mpadded voffset="-0.2pt"><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-1.01px" height="5.95" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 4.45 5.95" width="4.45"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#5C6269;" fill="#5C6269" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,5.95) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(2.23,0) translate(0,3.1)"> <path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z"></path> </g> </svg> </mtext></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\prod_{i\in\mathsf{Ag}}\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.2411pt}{\mbox{\hbox to3.22pt{\vbox to4.3pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.60818pt\lower-2.23749pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x^{\mathcal{C}}).</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Circular Compositional Soundness (restated))</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be a certified contract. For any contract-product execution
<math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{0}x_{1}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{1}\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mi>a</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{0}x_{1}^{\mathcal{C}}a_{1}\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> starting from <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> at every time <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, then every reachable contract product state remains in <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the local obligations hold along the execution, and the induced global trace satisfies <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is available in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A2.SS1" title="0.B.1 Proof of Theorem 1. Circular Compositional Soundness ‣ Appendix 0.B Technical Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.B.1</span></a>.
Informally, the theorem says that a certified circular contract behaves like a joint safety proof split across local masks. The invariant is simple: start inside the winning region, and every projected shield action keeps the next product state inside it. Thus, once the rectangle has been certified, the agents do not need any coordination — any joint action admitted by the local masks is still inside the certified successor region.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Learning with Contract Shields</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Building on Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, this section gives the concrete pipeline: bounded offline construction of a certified library in Section <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Library Construction: Bounded Certified Profile Search ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, its permissiveness and optimality interpretation in Section <a href="#S5.SS2" title="5.2 Permissiveness and Optimality ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a>, and online contract selection in Section <a href="#S5.SS3" title="5.3 Bandit Selector ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Library Construction: Bounded Certified Profile Search</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The finite contract search space <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, with candidates <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> drawn from the finite search space of
Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition4" title="Definition 4 (Finite Contract Search Space) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, so we enumerate candidate local-obligation tuples before learning and certify each tuple using the fixed-point construction above. For any finite ordered candidate family <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, the certified library induced by <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is
<math id="S5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}(\mathcal{F})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{F}\mid\mathcal{C}\ \text{is certified}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>is certified</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}(\mathcal{F})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{F}\mid\mathcal{C}\ \text{is certified}\},</annotation></semantics></math>
with the order inherited from <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> is finite, so is <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}(\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}(\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math>; moreover, membership in the library is exactly certification, so every retained contract satisfies the hypotheses of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Circular Compositional Soundness (restated)) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. The selector
therefore uses this catalogue of safe shield configurations without constructing or validating new safety certificates online. The algorithm enumerates scoped candidate subsets in a deterministic prioritised order subject to the configured profile limit and formula depth limit; this order uses a temporal-form heuristic that prefers persistent <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\psi</annotation></semantics></math> obligations before next-state <math id="S5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\psi</annotation></semantics></math> obligations. Algorithm <a href="#algorithm1" title="In 5.1 Library Construction: Bounded Certified Profile Search ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> summarises this finite preprocessing stage. Return-optimal behaviour does not necessarily arise from the first certified profile. A stricter contract can enable solving the decentralised learner’s coordination problem, so the learning-time selector optimises over the retained library.</p>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Certified profile library construction</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.4.1" class="ltx_listingline">
<span id="algorithm1.4.1.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> </span>ordered bounded profile family <math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}\subseteq\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, initial abstract states <math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, global safety formula <math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.2" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1" class="ltx_text"><span id="algorithm1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> </span>initial certified profile <math id="algorithm1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and certified library <math id="algorithm1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.3" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.4" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">foreach</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.4.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\varphi_{i}\rangle_{i=1}^{n}\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> in search order</em> <span id="algorithm1.4.4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.5" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.5.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}\not\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊧̸</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\not\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.6" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">continue</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.7" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> compile the local obligation automata <math id="algorithm1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{1}^{\mathcal{C}},\dots,\mathcal{A}_{n}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mn>1</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>n</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{1}^{\mathcal{C}},\dots,\mathcal{A}_{n}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.8" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> construct the contract product <math id="algorithm1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>X</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and greatest fixed point <math id="algorithm1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.9" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.9.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">every initial contract state induced by <math id="algorithm1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> lies in <math id="algorithm1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.10" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> derive the local shields from the certified rectangles <math id="algorithm1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathcal{C}}(x^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.11" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>  <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> add <math id="algorithm1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algorithm1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <em id="algorithm1.4.12.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic"><math id="algorithm1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math></em> <span id="algorithm1.4.12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.13" class="ltx_listingline"> <span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span> <span id="algorithm1.4.13.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> failure
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.14" class="ltx_listingline"><math id="algorithm1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}\leftarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}\leftarrow</annotation></semantics></math> the first profile in <math id="algorithm1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math> in certification order
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.4.15.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="algorithm1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="algorithm1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.4.16" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.2 </span>Permissiveness and Optimality</h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition14" title="Definition 14 (Cardinality Permissiveness) ‣ 5.2 Permissiveness and Optimality ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> gives a statewise mask-size metric, obtained simply by counting the sizes of local action masks relative to the protocol-available action sets.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Cardinality Permissiveness)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition14.p1.1" class="ltx_p">At a shield state <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,\bar{q})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\mathcal{C}}=(s,\bar{q})</annotation></semantics></math>, the cardinality permissiveness of
agent <math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s local mask is
<math id="Thmdefinition14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\frac{|\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.17221pt}{\mbox{\hbox to2.3pt{\vbox to3.07pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.14871pt\lower-1.59822pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
{}{}
{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}{{}}{}{{}}{}{}{}
{}{}
{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.04 L 1.59 1.35 L 1.24 -0.17 C 0.97 -1.28 0.31 -1.9 0 -2.21 C -0.31 -1.9 -0.97 -1.28 -1.24 -0.17 L -1.59 1.35 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})|}{|d^{i}(s)|}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mpadded voffset="-0.2pt"><mtext> <svg style="vertical-align:-0.72px" height="4.25" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 3.18 4.25" width="3.18"> <g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#5C6269;" fill="#5C6269" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,4.25) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(1.59,0) translate(0,2.21)"> <path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 2.04 L 1.59 1.35 L 1.24 -0.17 C 0.97 -1.28 0.31 -1.9 0 -2.21 C -0.31 -1.9 -0.97 -1.28 -1.24 -0.17 L -1.59 1.35 Z"></path> </g> </svg> </mtext></mpadded><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}(x^{\mathcal{C}})\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\frac{|\mathcal{M}_{\mathord{\raisebox{-0.17221pt}{\mbox{\hbox to2.3pt{\vbox to3.07pt{\pgfpicture\makeatletter\hbox{\hskip 1.14871pt\lower-1.59822pt\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke=#000000} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#000000} \lxSVG@setlinewidth{\the\pgflinewidth}\lxSVG@begingroup@{stroke-width=0.4pt} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\nullfont\hbox to0.0pt{\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces{{}{{}}{}
