{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\lxSVG@begingroup@{_scopebegin=1} \lxSVG@begingroup@{fill=#5C6269} \lxSVG@fill\lxSVG@drawpath@unclipped{M 0 2.85 L 2.23 1.89 L 1.74 -0.24 C 1.35 -1.79 0.44 -2.66 0 -3.1 C -0.44 -2.66 -1.35 -1.79 -1.74 -0.24 L -2.23 1.89 Z}{stroke:none} \lx@inpgf@ignorespaces
\lxSVG@closescope }
\lxSVG@closescope {\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces}\hss}\lxSVG@discardpath\lxSVG@closescope \hss}}\lxSVG@closescope\endpgfpicture}}}}}}^{\mathcal{C},i}(x^{\mathcal{C}^{\star}})=\{a^{i}_{\pi^{\star}}(s)\}\qquad\text{for every reachable }x^{\mathcal{C}^{\star}}=(s,\bar{q})\text{ and every }i\in\mathsf{Ag},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">then <math id="S5.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi^{\star}\in\Pi(\mathcal{C}^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi^{\star}\in\Pi(\mathcal{C}^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>, so Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Optimal Safe Recovery (restated)) ‣ 5.2 Permissiveness and Optimality ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> applies. The local masks also enforce the globally optimal safe joint action on all reachable states. These statements concern deterministic Markov optima. For the finite discounted, fully observable cooperative concurrent stochastic games considered in our setting, policy randomisation is not required to attain the optimal team value: an optimal deterministic Markov joint policy exists, although stochastic policies remain useful during learning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>, <a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">26</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.3 </span>Bandit Selector</h3>

<div id="S5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The learning-time selector is an outer loop over the certified library: it chooses which pre-certified contract (shield) governs each training block, while the inner MARL algorithm continues updating its policies under the currently active shields. Each certified contract is treated as an arm. Pulling arm <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> means training for one dwell block under <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>’s shield and measuring the resulting team return. The selector is parameterised by:</p>
<ul id="S5.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S5.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the finite certified library <math id="S5.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math> of candidate contracts;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the initial certified contract <math id="S5.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the warm-up horizon <math id="S5.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, measured in completed episodes;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the dwell length <math id="S5.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>, measured in completed episodes per arm pull;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the discount factor <math id="S5.I1.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> for historical block statistics; and</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S5.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S5.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">the exploration coefficient <math id="S5.I1.i6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> be the completed episodes in a dwell block <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> run under
contract <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{e}^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{e}^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> be the episode return of agent <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> in episode <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>e</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e</annotation></semantics></math>. The selector uses the normalised team-return score
<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{b}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\overline{R}_{b}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\frac{1}{|E_{b}|\,n}\sum_{e\in E_{b}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{e}^{i}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>R</mi><mo stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mi>b</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{b}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\overline{R}_{b}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\frac{1}{|E_{b}|\,n}\sum_{e\in E_{b}}\sum_{i=1}^{n}R_{e}^{i},</annotation></semantics></math>
which is equivalent to the usual team return up to the constant factor <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>. The resulting bandit is <em id="S5.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">non-stationary</em>: an arm’s payoff changes as the inner policies continue to learn under the active shields. Discounting therefore estimates recent block performance rather than a fixed stationary arm mean, following discounted UCB methods for non-stationary bandits <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. For each certified contract <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, maintain discounted count and score statistics <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. When a block under <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{b}</annotation></semantics></math> completes, all arms are first discounted by setting <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{C}}\leftarrow\eta N_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{C}}\leftarrow\eta N_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{\mathcal{C}}\leftarrow\eta S_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{\mathcal{C}}\leftarrow\eta S_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the observed arm is then updated by</p>
<table id="S5.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}\leftarrow N_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}+1,\qquad S_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}\leftarrow S_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}+y_{b},\qquad\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}S_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}/N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}\leftarrow N_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}+1,\qquad S_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}\leftarrow S_{\mathcal{C}_{b}}+y_{b},\qquad\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}S_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}/N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined for each <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. After
<math id="S5.SS3.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> completed warm-up episodes under <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, the selector accumulates dwell blocks of <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> completed episodes, tries certified contracts whose identifiers have not yet been visited, then choosing</p>
<table id="S5.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S5.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{b+1}\in\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}\\
N_{\mathcal{C}}&gt;0\end{subarray}}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}}+\beta\sqrt{\frac{\log(1+\max\{1,\sum_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}\})}{N_{\mathcal{C}}}}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{b+1}\in\arg\max_{\begin{subarray}{c}\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}\\
N_{\mathcal{C}}&gt;0\end{subarray}}\left(\widehat{\mu}_{\mathcal{C}}+\beta\sqrt{\frac{\log(1+\max\{1,\sum_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}N_{\mathcal{C}^{\prime}}\})}{N_{\mathcal{C}}}}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S5.SS3.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> is the exploration coefficient. Ties are resolved deterministically, preferring to keep the current contract and otherwise using the certified-library order. Algorithm <a href="#algorithm2" title="In Policies and shielded controllers. ‣ Appendix 0.E Technical Remarks ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A5" title="Appendix 0.E Technical Remarks ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.E</span></a> gives the discounted-UCB update.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 5.2</span></span><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Safety of Certified Selection (restated))</span></h6>
<div id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math> be a certified library. Consider any sequence of episodes in which each episode is assigned a contract <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>, starts from an initial product state covered by <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math>’s certification, the shield for <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is deployed for the whole episode, every generated joint action lies in <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> at the current contract product state, and contract switches occur only at episode reset boundaries. Then no generated episode prefix is a bad prefix of the global safety objective. Under the standard per-episode infinite-trace semantics, every episode satisfies <math id="S5.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proof is available in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A2.SS3" title="0.B.3 Proof of Theorem 3. Certified Selection Safety ‣ Appendix 0.B Technical Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.B.3</span></a>. Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Safety of Certified Selection (restated)) ‣ 5.3 Bandit Selector ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> allows the selector to adapt reward estimates and switch contracts between episodes, but it never admits an uncertified tuple. Thus the outer loop can optimise team return over the finite space of certified contracts while preserving deterministic safety. Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Safety of Certified Selection (restated)) ‣ 5.3 Bandit Selector ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a> does not by itself give a convergence guarantee for the discounted bandit selector; the optimal safe team return is attainable only insofar as it is represented by some certified contract in the library and the learning dynamics select the corresponding profile. Without that representability assumption, performance is limited by the expressive power of the contract language and certified library.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Empirical Evaluation</h2>

<div id="S6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report the experimental configuration, benchmark suite, certified search counts, and learning curves. Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A3" title="Appendix 0.C Environments ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.C</span></a> gives environment details, labelling, and safety objectives; Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A4" title="Appendix 0.D Extended Experimental Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.D</span></a> reports full curves. The implementation is open-source and available at <a href="https://github.com/nightly/contract-shielding" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/nightly/contract-shielding</a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Implementation Details and Hyperparameters.</h5>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The formal development uses a single global alphabet <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ap}</annotation></semantics></math> and global labelling function <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. For tractability, the implementation stores per-agent sub-alphabets <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ap}_{i}\subseteq\mathsf{Ap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ap}_{i}\subseteq\mathsf{Ap}</annotation></semantics></math> and compiles each local automaton over <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{i}=2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{i}=2^{\mathsf{Ap}_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math>; automaton <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> receives label <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(s)\cap\mathsf{Ap}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(s)\cap\mathsf{Ap}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> at state <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>. Certification checks consistency with the global model: each <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ap}_{i}\subseteq\mathsf{Ap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⊆</mo><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ap}_{i}\subseteq\mathsf{Ap}</annotation></semantics></math>, each local label is the corresponding projection, and propositions shared by multiple local alphabets agree, see Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition3" title="Definition 3 (Contract) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. We bound candidate formula depth by <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=2</annotation></semantics></math> (interpreting atoms as <math id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=1</annotation></semantics></math>). Other hyperparameters are given in Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A6" title="Appendix 0.F Hyperparameters ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algorithms.</h5>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare independent learners (<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IPPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>]</cite>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IQL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">27</a>]</cite>), centralised-critic or value-decomposition learners (<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MAPPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">30</a>]</cite>,
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Joint-PPO</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">PQN-VDN</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">25</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>), Lagrangian variants of <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IPPO</span> and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IQL</span>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, ordinary shielded variants, and
<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Contract-IPPO</span>/<span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Contract-IQL</span>. <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MAPPO</span> uses a centralised critic with decentralised actors; <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Joint-PPO</span> and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Shielded-Joint-PPO</span> use centralised actors and critics and serve as upper-end reward baselines although outside our decentralised-execution setting.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Environments.</h5>

<div id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation covered six cooperative MARL benchmarks: <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Connector</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Level-Based Foraging</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RWARE</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>, <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, and <span id="S6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Car Platoon</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. Example <a href="#Thmexample2" title="Example 2 ‣ Environments. ‣ 6 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> illustrates one safety property and contract; Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A3" title="Appendix 0.C Environments ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.C</span></a> expands the rest.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmexample2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_example">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmexample2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example 2</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmexample2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmexample2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In <span id="Thmexample2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span>, 2 holder agents open doors by standing on assigned plates while a runner crosses to the goal. Let <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> be goal achievement; let <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> mean that the runner is in door <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, after door <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and able to return before door <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>; and let <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> mean that holder <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> has not abandoned plate <math id="Thmexample2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> before the goal. The holder obligations let the runner’s mask rely on held doors when admitting crossings; factorised masks must be robust to holder departures, so they conservatively keep the runner out of the protected door regions. The default return-route objective and one certified local contract are</p>
<table id="S6.Ex16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S6.Ex16X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗉𝗉</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\!\bigwedge_{k=0}^{1}\bigl((\neg Z\wedge(I_{k}\vee A_{k}))\rightarrow B_{k}\bigr)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.580em;" width="0.580em"><mi>𝖦</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\!\bigwedge_{k=0}^{1}\bigl((\neg Z\wedge(I_{k}\vee A_{k}))\rightarrow B_{k}\bigr),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S6.Ex16Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{C}^{\mathsf{pp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>𝗉𝗉</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{C}^{\mathsf{pp}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S6.Ex16Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\mathsf{G}H_{0},\ \mathsf{G}H_{1},\ \Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗉𝗉</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\langle\mathsf{G}H_{0},\ \mathsf{G}H_{1},\ \Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
