<section id="Pt0.Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

<div id="Pt0.Ax1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The appendix is organised as follows:</p>
<ul id="Pt0.Ax1.I1" class="ltx_itemize" style="--ltx-enum-leftmargin:0pt;">
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A1" title="Appendix 0.A Safe LTL Semantics ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.A</span></a>: <math id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math> semantics are provided.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A2" title="Appendix 0.B Technical Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.B</span></a>: Technical results and proofs are provided.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A3" title="Appendix 0.C Environments ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.C</span></a>: Environment-level benchmark details are provided.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A4" title="Appendix 0.D Extended Experimental Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.D</span></a>: Complete experimental results are reported.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A5" title="Appendix 0.E Technical Remarks ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.E</span></a>: Technical remarks on contract selection are provided.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"> 
<div id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.Ax1.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Appendix <a href="#Pt0.A6" title="Appendix 0.F Hyperparameters ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">0.F</span></a>: Hyperparameters are provided for replication.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.A </span>Safe LTL Semantics</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="Pt0.A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>ω</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(2^{\mathsf{Ap}})^{\omega}</annotation></semantics></math> be the set of traces over <math id="Pt0.A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Ap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖠𝗉</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Ap}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we can define the inductive semantics used in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Preliminaries ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="351.64" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 351.64" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,351.64) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 1.31 L 0 350.32 C 0 351.05 0.59 351.64 1.31 351.64 L 476.06 351.64 C 476.79 351.64 477.38 351.05 477.38 350.32 L 477.38 1.31 C 477.38 0.59 476.79 0 476.06 0 L 1.31 0 C 0.59 0 0 0.59 0 1.31 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F5F5;" fill="#F5F5F5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.31 1.31 L 1.31 350.32 L 476.06 350.32 L 476.06 1.31 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 1.31 172.36)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:34.31em;--ltx-fo-height:12.63em;--ltx-fo-depth:12.13em;font-size:10pt;" class="ltx_minipage" height="342.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 174.82)" width="43.04em"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<table id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_l ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-bottom: -0.45206pt;padding:-0.15pt 0.0pt;" colspan="3">
<span id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:336.3pt;"><span class="ltx_rule ltx_align_left" style="width:0.0pt;height:7.4pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span>
<span id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p ltx_align_left"><span id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_sansserif ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:80%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For any trace <math id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, position <math id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and formulae <math id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi,\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi,\psi</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="Pt0.A1.p2.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:-0.15pt 0.0pt;" colspan="3"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:100%;height:0.4pt;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;--ltx-bg-color:#000000;display:inline-block;"> </span></td></tr>
