<section id="Pt0.A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.B </span>Technical Results</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides all of the formal proofs of results stated in the main text.</p>
</div>
<section id="Pt0.A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.B.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1. Circular Compositional Soundness</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Circular Compositional Soundness (restated)) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We prove the invariant <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> by induction on time (establishing the invariant for all <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>). The base case is exactly the second certification condition, <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the step case, assume <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> and write <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the executed joint action satisfies
<math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>, Definitions <a href="#Thmdefinition11" title="Definition 11 (Projected Local Shield) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and <a href="#Thmdefinition13" title="Definition 13 (Admitted Joint Actions) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> give</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}\in\prod_{i\in\mathsf{Ag}}R_{\mathcal{C}}^{i}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})=R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝖠𝗀</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}\in\prod_{i\in\mathsf{Ag}}R_{\mathcal{C}}^{i}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})=R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">By the choice of the certified rectangle,
<math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})\in\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})=\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}},x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖼𝗍</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})\in\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})=\mathsf{Rect}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}},x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math> is a <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>-closed local action rectangle at <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>; in particular, <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is legal at <math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t})\subseteq\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>Post</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t})\subseteq\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Every possible next product state
<math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is in this successor set, hence
<math id="Thmproofx1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}=\mathcal{T}_{\mathcal{C}}(\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>, every state in
<math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is locally safe. For each agent <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and time <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, the automaton component of <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="q_{i,t}=\delta_{i}^{\ast}(q_{i}^{0},\ell_{i}(s_{0})\ell_{i}(s_{1})\cdots\ell_{i}(s_{t}))," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i,t}=\delta_{i}^{\ast}(q_{i}^{0},\ell_{i}(s_{0})\ell_{i}(s_{1})\cdots\ell_{i}(s_{t})),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproofx1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">by the definition of the contract product. Since <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i,t}\notin B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i,t}\notin B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, no finite prefix of the projected local trace is a bad prefix. By Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition6" title="Definition 6 (Contract Safety Automata) ‣ 4.1 Assume-Guarantee Contracts ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, the projected local trace satisfies <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varphi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varphi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for every agent <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The lifted entailment condition <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊧</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">↑</mo></msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\models_{\!\uparrow}\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math> in
Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition10" title="Definition 10 (Certified Contract) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> then implies that the global trace satisfies <math id="Thmproofx1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.B.2 </span>Proof of Theorem 2. Optimal Safe Recovery</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (Optimal Safe Recovery (restated)) ‣ 5.2 Permissiveness and Optimality ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix any certified <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math> and any
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi(\mathcal{C})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi(\mathcal{C})</annotation></semantics></math>. We show that every contract-product execution consistent with
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> uses only admitted actions. The initial product state is in
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖼𝗁</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> by definition. If
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})\in\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>q</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖼𝗁</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}}=(s_{t},\bar{q}_{t})\in\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>, compatibility gives
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Supp(\pi(\cdot\mid s_{t}))\subseteq\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Supp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Supp(\pi(\cdot\mid s_{t}))\subseteq\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>; therefore every
action chosen with positive probability by <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is admitted. For any
successor <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Post</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathrm{Post}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}},a_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, closure of
<math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖼𝗁</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖱𝖾𝖺𝖼𝗁</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t+1}^{\mathcal{C}}\in\mathsf{Reach}_{\mathcal{C}}(\pi)</annotation></semantics></math>. By induction,
all actions along every execution consistent with <math id="Thmproofx2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> are admitted by the
deployed shields.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Circular Compositional Soundness (restated)) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> then implies that every such
execution satisfies <math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Thus every feasible pair <math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{C},\pi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{C},\pi)</annotation></semantics></math> in the certified-shield optimisation has
value at most
<math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\mathsf{safe}}}J_{s_{0}}(\pi)=J_{s_{0}}(\pi^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi\in\Pi_{\mathsf{safe}}}J_{s_{0}}(\pi)=J_{s_{0}}(\pi^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. Conversely,
by the hypothesis, the feasible pair <math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathcal{C}^{\star},\pi^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathcal{C}^{\star},\pi^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math> attains
<math id="Thmproofx2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{s_{0}}(\pi^{\star})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><msub><mi>s</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{s_{0}}(\pi^{\star})</annotation></semantics></math>. The two inequalities give the claimed equality.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.B.3 </span>Proof of Theorem 3. Certified Selection Safety</h3>

<div id="Pt0.A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">See <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 5.2 (Safety of Certified Selection (restated)) ‣ 5.3 Bandit Selector ‣ 5 Learning with Contract Shields ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.2</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproofx3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproofx3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof</span></span></h6>
<div id="Thmproofx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproofx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Fix an arbitrary episode and let <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> be its assigned contract. Since
<math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>𝖼𝖾𝗋𝗍</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\in\mathcal{L}_{\mathsf{cert}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the definition of the certified library gives
that <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is certified. By hypothesis, the episode begins at an initial contract
product state in <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the shield for <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is used for every
step of the episode with generated actions in <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖠𝖽𝗆</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Adm}_{\mathcal{C}}(x_{t}^{\mathcal{C}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1 (Circular Compositional Soundness (restated)) ‣ 4.2 Contract Product Shields ‣ 4 Contract Shielding ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>
therefore applies throughout the episode: all reachable contract product states
remain in <math id="Thmproofx3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖶𝗂𝗇</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{Win}^{\Box}_{\mathcal{C}}</annotation></semantics></math>, no contract safety automaton reaches a
bad state, and the global safety objective is satisfied. Hence no generated
episode prefix is a bad prefix of the global safety objective. Because switches occur only between episodes, the
same argument restarts independently for each selected contract.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.C </span>Environments</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides details for all of the environments considered in our empirical evaluation of Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. We use finite safety abstractions for contract and shield synthesis. For the safety game, the abstraction is required to preserve the successor support relevant to the automata and the truth of all propositions appearing in the global and local obligations.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#Pt0.A3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix 0.C Environments ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows renders of the
six benchmark environments described below.</p>
</div>
