<span id="Pt0.A3.F5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps" style="font-size:80%;">Car Platoon<span id="Pt0.A3.F5.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>Renders of the six benchmark environments used in the evaluation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.1 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span> is a role-structured grid task. Let
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{0,\dots,H-1\}\times\{0,\dots,W-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\{0,\dots,H-1\}\times\{0,\dots,W-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the grid, let <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}n-1</annotation></semantics></math> be the number of doors and plates, and let agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-1</annotation></semantics></math> be the runner. An abstract state is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},C,b_{0},\dots,b_{m-1},o_{0},\dots,o_{m-1},g,V_{H},V_{W},t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},C,b_{0},\dots,b_{m-1},o_{0},\dots,o_{m-1},g,V_{H},V_{W},t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in G</annotation></semantics></math> is an agent position, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\subseteq\{0,\dots,m-1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\subseteq\{0,\dots,m-1\}</annotation></semantics></math> is a
one-step latch recording doors crossed by the runner on the preceding transition, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{k},o_{k},g\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>o</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{k},o_{k},g\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> record whether plate <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is pressed, door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is open, and the goal is reached, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{H}</annotation></semantics></math> records door-holder protocol
violations, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{W}</annotation></semantics></math> records runner wait-for-door violations, and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the step
count. Each agent has primitive actions
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{Up},\mathsf{Down},\mathsf{Left},\mathsf{Right},\mathsf{Noop}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴𝗉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖣𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖫𝖾𝖿𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖱𝗂𝗀𝗁𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗈𝗉</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{Up},\mathsf{Down},\mathsf{Left},\mathsf{Right},\mathsf{Noop}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The transition samples a permutation of the agents, applies their proposed moves sequentially, and cancels moves into grid boundaries, walls, closed doors, or occupied cells. After movement, plate <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is pressed iff the assigned holder <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> occupies it, and door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> is open iff that plate is pressed.
The latch <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> contains door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> exactly when the runner entered a cell of door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, left such a cell toward the far side, or crossed the door boundary during the transition; it is empty on non-crossing transitions. The episode terminates when some agent reaches the goal or the horizon is met.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rewards are role-shaped: holders receive dense shaping toward their assigned
plates, while the runner is shaped toward the goal. The reported experiments
use distance normalisation <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\max}=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\max}=10</annotation></semantics></math>, step cost <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, and goal bonus
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For holder <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i&lt;m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i&lt;m</annotation></semantics></math>, the local contract alphabet contains its door-holding proposition, door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> open and plate-pressed propositions, holder-on-plate propositions, goal achievement, and the runner’s waiting, crossing, in-door, and after-door phase propositions for door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>. The runner’s local alphabet contains, for every door, its wait-for-door, waiting, crossing, in-door,
after-door, door-open, and return-route propositions, together with goal achievement. The global alphabet contains these propositions and the finite agent-cell, agent-at-goal, agent-before-door, and plate/door status propositions needed to interpret the benchmark labels.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The default benchmark instance uses the linear layout with <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=7</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W=4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=3</annotation></semantics></math>, sensor range <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, and horizon <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="150" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>150</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">150</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> respectively abbreviate the runner-after-door, runner-in-door, runner-can-return
before door, and goal-achieved propositions. The default safety formula is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\bigwedge_{k\in\{0,1\}}\bigl((\neg Z\wedge(I_{k}\vee A_{k}))\rightarrow B_{k}\bigr)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗉𝗉</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">¬</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\bigwedge_{k\in\{0,1\}}\bigl((\neg Z\wedge(I_{k}\vee A_{k}))\rightarrow B_{k}\bigr).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">The return-route label <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is computed by reachability from the runner’s current cell to a cell before door <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, treating walls and closed doors as blocked and ignoring teammate occupancy. A direct generic per-agent shield for this formula is not realisable from the initial state, so the ordinary shielded
baseline uses the conservative runner-only formulas</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="Pt0.A3.Ex22X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\top," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊤</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\top,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\top," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⊤</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\top,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varphi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>φ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varphi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex22Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\neg(I_{0}\vee A_{0}\vee I_{1}\vee A_{1})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∨</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\mathsf{G}\neg(I_{0}\vee A_{0}\vee I_{1}\vee A_{1}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">while the global automaton still checks <math id="Pt0.A3.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗉𝗉</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{pp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Certified contract profiles can instead assign holder obligations that preserve
the runner’s return route while the runner carries the global return-route
obligation.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.2 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RWARE</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RWARE</span> is a warehouse queue and delivery benchmark. A state is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(u_{1},\dots,u_{n},\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{q},Q,Y,t,\iota)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ι</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(u_{1},\dots,u_{n},\sigma_{1},\dots,\sigma_{q},Q,Y,t,\iota),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(x_{i},y_{i},d_{i},\ell_{i},c_{i},h_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(x_{i},y_{i},d_{i},\ell_{i},c_{i},h_{i})</annotation></semantics></math> records robot position, direction,
loaded status, whether the carried shelf is requested, and whether a delivery
has occurred; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> records shelf identities and positions; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is the
request queue; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> records standing and requested shelf locations; and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,\iota" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ι</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,\iota</annotation></semantics></math>
are the total and inactive step counts. Each robot has actions
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{NOOP},\mathsf{FORWARD},\mathsf{LEFT},\mathsf{RIGHT},\mathsf{TOGGLE\_LOAD}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝖮𝖮𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖥𝖮𝖱𝖶𝖠𝖱𝖣</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖫𝖤𝖥𝖳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖱𝖨𝖦𝖧𝖳</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖳𝖮𝖦𝖦𝖫𝖤</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖫𝖮𝖠𝖣</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{NOOP},\mathsf{FORWARD},\mathsf{LEFT},\mathsf{RIGHT},\mathsf{TOGGLE\_LOAD}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Turning updates <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, forward movement requests the
cell in direction <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and load toggling picks up or drops a shelf when the
warehouse interaction is legal. The transition resolves collisions using
separate robot and shelf occupancy layers; a loaded robot occupies both layers.
When a requested shelf reaches a goal cell, the request is replaced by a new
request according to the environment kernel.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rewards are sparse and delivery based: in the default individual reward mode,
robot <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> receives reward only when it delivers a requested shelf, with no
movement reward or direct penalty for protocol violations.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The local contract alphabet for robot <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains the
queue-yield proposition <span id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">agent_i_queue_yield_ok</span>. The proposition is
false on a transition precisely when robot <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> is unloaded, occupies the next
forward cell of a robot carrying a requested shelf in the queue, and remains in
that blocking cell after joint-action execution and collision resolution.
The global alphabet additionally contains finite robot-position propositions,
highway and zone-membership propositions, loaded and carrying-requested status,
requested-shelf locations and at-requested-shelf facts, requested-carrier
status, blocking-requested-carrier facts, and delivery-lane and
requested-carrier-progress protocol propositions.
Writing <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_queue\_yield\_ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">agent_i_queue_yield_ok</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_queue\_yield\_ok}</annotation></semantics></math>, the default safety formula is
the per-robot queue-yield invariant</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{rw}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}q_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗋𝗐</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{rw}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}q_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The default queue-conflict instance uses <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, shelf columns <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, column
height <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math>, one shelf row, sensor range <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, flattened observations, request
queue size <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, individual rewards, no inactivity cutoff, and horizon <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="200" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>200</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">200</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Ordinary factorised shielding is not realisable for this default queue-yield
objective. The proposition <math id="Pt0.A3.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> records a joint transition fact. A factorised
shield exposes independent local action sets, so every combination of
individually permitted actions must remain safe against arbitrary teammate
choices. In the queue-conflict layout, reachable states can require the blocker
and carrier to take compatible same-step actions; no single local blocker action
is certified safe against all carrier actions, and the projected local mask can
become empty. Contract shields avoid this failure by first certifying teammate
obligations, so local masks are checked against obligation-constrained teammates
rather than the full adversarial action set.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.3 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Connector</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Connector</span> is a grid routing task. A state is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(B,p_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},z_{0},\dots,z_{n-1},V,t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(B,p_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},z_{0},\dots,z_{n-1},V,t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\in\{0,\dots,3n\}^{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>G</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\in\{0,\dots,3n\}^{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is the grid of empty cells, trails, current
positions, and targets; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i},z_{i}\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i},z_{i}\in G</annotation></semantics></math> are current and target cells; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> records
reservation violations; and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the step count. Each agent has actions
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{Noop},\mathsf{Up},\mathsf{Right},\mathsf{Down},\mathsf{Left}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝗈𝗈𝗉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖴𝗉</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖱𝗂𝗀𝗁𝗍</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖣𝗈𝗐𝗇</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖫𝖾𝖿𝗍</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{Noop},\mathsf{Up},\mathsf{Right},\mathsf{Down},\mathsf{Left}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The action mask permits a movement only into an empty cell or the agent’s own
target; illegal actions have no movement effect. Simultaneous proposed moves
are computed from the current positions. Destination conflicts are resolved by a
fixed agent-index priority rule: an agent whose proposed destination is
also proposed by a later-indexed agent is cancelled, while successful moves
leave a path marker behind, and reaching the target changes the target marker
into the agent position marker. The episode terminates when all agents are
connected or blocked, or when the horizon is met.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Dense rewards give each unconnected agent a connection bonus and a per-step
cost until it reaches its target. The default constants are
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathsf{conn}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝖼𝗈𝗇𝗇</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathsf{conn}}=1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\mathsf{step}}=-0.03" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>𝗌𝗍𝖾𝗉</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\mathsf{step}}=-0.03</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The local contract alphabet for agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains its aggregate
reservation-respect and route-clearance propositions, pairwise propositions
stating that agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> keeps another agent’s reserved route clear and respects
that agent’s reservation, and every agent’s reserved-route-clear proposition.
The global alphabet contains finite current-position and target-position
propositions, action-availability propositions, connection and blocked status,
reserved-route-blocked and on-reserved-route propositions, and the aggregate and
pairwise reservation-respect and route-clearance propositions. Let
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_reserved\_route\_clear\_ok}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">agent_i_reserved_route_clear_ok</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_reserved\_route\_clear\_ok}</annotation></semantics></math>. The default safety formula is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{co}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}r_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝖼𝗈</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{co}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}r_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The default reservation-conflict experiment uses the
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">reservation_priority_conflict</span> generator with fixed layout seed <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>,
a <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math> grid, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, dense rewards, the reserved cell <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(2,2)</annotation></semantics></math> for
agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and horizon <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Ordinary factorised shielding is not realisable for this default
reserved-route-clearance objective. The proposition <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is owned by
agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> but can be falsified by a teammate entering or remaining on
agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>’s reserved route. A local shield for the route owner must therefore
be safe against all teammate actions, yet the owner has no action that can force
the teammate off its reserved cells. Conversely, the teammate’s factorised mask
cannot express the conditional commitment “avoid the owner’s reserved route
while the owner is still unconnected” unless that commitment appears as part
of a certified contract profile. The Cartesian product of ordinary local masks
therefore cannot deploy a non-empty shield that preserves the global
route-clearance invariant from the reservation-priority layout, whereas a
contract profile can add explicit reservation-respect obligations.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.4 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span> is a railway-routing benchmark. A state is
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(\xi_{0},\dots,\xi_{n-1},D,C,V,t)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(\xi_{0},\dots,\xi_{n-1},D,C,V,t),</annotation></semantics></math>
where each train state
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{i},d_{i},\kappa_{i},z_{i},p_{i}^{0},d_{i}^{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{i},d_{i},\kappa_{i},z_{i},p_{i}^{0},d_{i}^{0})</annotation></semantics></math> contains current position, direction,
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span> train status, target, and initial placement; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of
deadlocked trains; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of trains stopped by conflicts; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> records
pairwise yield violations; and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the elapsed step count. The primitive
actions are the five <span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span> rail actions: do nothing, turn left, move
forward, turn right, and stop. The transition is <span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span>’s
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">RailEnv</span> transition restricted by the rail graph, train status, malfunctions, and conflict resolution. In the single-track benchmark this transition is deterministic after the fixed scenario is generated.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Progress rewards give credit for reducing shortest-path distance to the target,
with a per-step cost, arrival bonus, and deadlock penalty. The default
constants are <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathsf{prog}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝗉𝗋𝗈𝗀</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathsf{prog}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathsf{step}}=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝗌𝗍𝖾𝗉</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathsf{step}}=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathsf{arr}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝖺𝗋𝗋</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathsf{arr}}=5</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mathsf{dead}}=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>𝖽𝖾𝖺𝖽</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mathsf{dead}}=5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The local contract alphabet for train <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains all trains’ deadlock
propositions and the pairwise yield propositions
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">agent_i_yields_to_agent_j_ok</span> for <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\neq i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\neq i</annotation></semantics></math>. The global alphabet
contains finite train-position propositions, target and off-map status,
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Flatland</span> train-status propositions, deadlock and conflict-stop
propositions, and pairwise yield-protocol propositions. The default safety
formula is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{fl}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}\neg(\texttt{agent\_i\_deadlocked})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝖿𝗅</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">agent_i_deadlocked</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{fl}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}\neg(\texttt{agent\_i\_deadlocked}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The default instance is <span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">single_track_meet</span> with <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, grid
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7\times 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7\times 3</annotation></semantics></math>, unit-speed trains, tree depth <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, predictor depth <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>,
progress rewards, <span id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">team_done</span> termination, no malfunctions, and the
horizon is <math id="Pt0.A3.SS4.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="12" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>12</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">12</annotation></semantics></math>. Candidate contracts can add pairwise yield obligations while preserving the global no-deadlock objective.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.5 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Level-Based Foraging</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Level-Based Foraging</span> models cooperative loading. A state is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{0},\ell_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},\ell_{n-1},F,V_{F},V_{S},V_{L},V_{C},t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>F</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(p_{0},\ell_{0},\dots,p_{n-1},\ell_{n-1},F,V_{F},V_{S},V_{L},V_{C},t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\in G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\in G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are agent positions and levels; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> is the finite
set of food triples <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y,\ell)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y,\ell)</annotation></semantics></math>; <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{F},V_{S},V_{L},V_{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{F},V_{S},V_{L},V_{C}</annotation></semantics></math> record failed loads,
successful loads, load attempts, and cooperative-load protocol violations; and
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the step count. Each agent has actions
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathsf{NONE},\mathsf{NORTH},\mathsf{SOUTH},\mathsf{WEST},\mathsf{EAST},\mathsf{LOAD}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭𝖮𝖭𝖤</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖭𝖮𝖱𝖳𝖧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖲𝖮𝖴𝖳𝖧</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖶𝖤𝖲𝖳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖤𝖠𝖲𝖳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝖫𝖮𝖠𝖣</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathsf{NONE},\mathsf{NORTH},\mathsf{SOUTH},\mathsf{WEST},\mathsf{EAST},\mathsf{LOAD}\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Invalid state-dependent actions become
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{NONE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖭𝖮𝖭𝖤</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{NONE}</annotation></semantics></math>, movement conflicts cancel all colliding moves, and a
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LOAD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖫𝖮𝖠𝖣</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LOAD}</annotation></semantics></math> action affects a food item only when the loader is adjacent to
that food. If the total level of adjacent loaders is below the food level, the
load fails; otherwise the food is collected.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Rewards are assigned only by loading: failed load attempts are penalised, and
successful loads give level-weighted credit to participating agents, normalised
by the total spawned food level in the default configuration.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The local contract alphabet for agent <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">agent_i_coop_load_ok</span> and every agent’s failed-load proposition.
The global alphabet contains food-availability, all-food-collected,
joint-load-ready, food-position, and food-level propositions, together with
finite agent-position propositions and per-agent load-attempt, successful-load,
failed-load, cooperative-load, adjacent-food, needs-partner,
partner-adjacent-same-food, and can-load-solo propositions. The default safety
formula is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{lbf}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}\neg(\texttt{agent\_i\_failed\_load})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝗅𝖻𝖿</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>¬</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">agent_i_failed_load</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{lbf}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}\neg(\texttt{agent\_i\_failed\_load}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p">The default experiment uses a <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 5</annotation></semantics></math> field, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=2</annotation></semantics></math>, one level-<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> food item,
two level-<math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> agents, <span id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">force_coop=true</span>, normalised rewards,
failed-load penalty <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, sight radius <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>, fixed layout seed <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, vector
observations, and horizon <math id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math>.
Candidate contracts can add cooperative-load obligations using
<span id="Pt0.A3.SS5.p3.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">agent_i_coop_load_ok</span> while preserving the global no-failed-load
objective.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">0.C.6 </span><span id="Pt0.A3.SS6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Car Platoon</span></h3>

<div id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Car Platoon</span> has one uncontrolled lead car and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=N-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=N-1</annotation></semantics></math> controlled followers, and is based on the environment described in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>. Cars are ordered front to back. A state is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(v_{0},\dots,v_{N-1},d_{0},\dots,d_{n-1},\Delta_{0},\dots,\Delta_{N-1},V_{C},V_{S},t)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}(v_{0},\dots,v_{N-1},d_{0},\dots,d_{n-1},\Delta_{0},\dots,\Delta_{N-1},V_{C},V_{S},t),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> is car velocity, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the following gap between car <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> and
car <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i+1</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> records damage, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{C},V_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>S</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{C},V_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> record conservative-follow and
smooth-lead protocol violations, and <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> is the step count. Controlled agents
choose brake, coast, or accelerate, mapped to accelerations <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-2,0,2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-2,0,2</annotation></semantics></math>, while the
lead car follows a velocity-dependent stochastic policy. Velocities are clipped
to <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[v_{\min},v_{\max}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[v_{\min},v_{\max}]</annotation></semantics></math>, and each gap is updated by trapezoidal integration of
relative velocity:</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}^{\prime}=d_{i}+\frac{(v_{i}-v_{i+1})+(v_{i}^{\prime}-v_{i+1}^{\prime})}{2}\Delta t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}^{\prime}=d_{i}+\frac{(v_{i}-v_{i+1})+(v_{i}^{\prime}-v_{i+1}^{\prime})}{2}\Delta t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Contact damages the adjacent cars, and a gap is unsafe when
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}^{\prime}\leq d_{\min}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}^{\prime}\leq d_{\min}</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}^{\prime}\geq d_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}^{\prime}\geq d_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>. Rewards penalise large following
gaps and unsafe-gap violations.
The default experiment uses <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t=1</annotation></semantics></math>, velocity bounds
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[v_{\min},v_{\max}]=[0,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[v_{\min},v_{\max}]=[0,2]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\min}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\min}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\max}=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\max}=20</annotation></semantics></math>, initial gap <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math>,
safety-violation penalty <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math>, and termination on violation.</p>
</div>
<div id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The local contract alphabet for controlled follower <math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> contains its gap-safe,
conservative-follow, and smooth-lead protocol propositions. The global alphabet
contains discretised velocity, front-velocity, and following-distance
propositions for each controlled follower, together with gap-safe, crashed,
too-far, near-boundary, closing/opening-fast
safe-to-accelerate-if-front-coasts, damage, and protocol propositions. Writing
<math id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_gap\_safe}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mover accent="true"><mo>=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">agent_i_gap_safe</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\texttt{agent\_i\_gap\_safe}</annotation></semantics></math>, the default safety formula is</p>
<table id="Pt0.A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="Pt0.A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi^{\mathsf{cp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}g_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi><mi>𝖼𝗉</mi></msubsup><mover accent="true"><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo mathsize="0.700em">def</mo></mover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⋀</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mi>𝖦</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi^{\mathsf{cp}}_{\mathsf{safe}}\mathrel{\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}}\bigwedge_{i=0}^{n-1}\mathsf{G}g_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Pt0.A3.SS6.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Candidate contracts can add conservative-follow or smooth-lead obligations
while keeping this global gap-safety objective fixed.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix 0.D </span>Extended Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="Pt0.A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix reports the extended empirical material omitted from the main paper. For each benchmark, the extended results record complete learning curves, safety-violation counts, shield-intervention statistics, and certified-contract selection traces when multiple certified profiles are available. Experiments were run on a Linux workstation with an AMD EPYC 7702P 64-core CPU and 64 logical cores and 203.48 GiB system RAM, and a single NVIDIA A16 GPU with 14.6 GiB memory.
Table <a href="#Pt0.A4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix 0.D Extended Experimental Results ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> reports the global safety objectives, bounded-search profile counts, and additional-obligation profile counts used in the main
evaluation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<div id="Pt0.A4.T1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:90.5pt;vertical-align:-44.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-64.3pt,16.9pt) scale(0.7,0.7) ;">
