<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Safety objectives are shown as global <math id="Pt0.A4.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖫𝖳𝖫</mi><mi>𝗌𝖺𝖿𝖾</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{LTL}_{\mathsf{safe}}</annotation></semantics></math> formulae alongside exported bounded-search profile counts. The final column counts retained profiles whose obligations are stricter than the global safety formula. For <span id="Pt0.A4.T1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span>, <math id="Pt0.A4.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A4.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A4.T1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Pt0.A4.T1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> abbreviate goal achievement, runner in-door, runner after-door, and runner return-route propositions.
</figcaption>
</figure>
