<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;">online TD target</span></span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">Exploration schedule</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" alttext="\epsilon:1.0\to 0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" lspace="0.278em" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">1.0</mn><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">0.05</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon:1.0\to 0.05</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;"> over <math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="80\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">80</mn><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" mathsize="1.430em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">80\%</annotation></semantics></math> of updates</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" alttext="\epsilon:1.0\to 0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" lspace="0.278em" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">1.0</mn><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">0.1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon:1.0\to 0.1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.8.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;"> over <math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF">10</mn><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathbackground="#FFFFFF" mathsize="1.430em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\%</annotation></semantics></math> of updates</span></span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;">Other settings</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;">double Q-learning enabled; replay size <math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;" mathbackground="#F7F7F7">50,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50{,}000</annotation></semantics></math></span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T7.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.9.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;">agent id appended; VDN team reward is summed; <math id="Pt0.A6.T7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;" mathbackground="#F7F7F7">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;" mathbackground="#F7F7F7">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-bg-color:#F7F7F7;" mathbackground="#F7F7F7">0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>; dueling disabled</span></span></span>
</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></p>
</span></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Value-based learner hyperparameters.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Constrained settings.</h5>

<div id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The constrained baselines use safety violations as cost signal, cost limit <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and cost discount <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{c}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{c}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>. Both
Lagrangian methods initialise the multiplier at <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and update it with step
size <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.05</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.05</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IPPO-Lagrangian</span> clips the multiplier to <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,10^{6}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,10^{6}]</annotation></semantics></math>, uses
cost GAE parameter <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}=0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.95</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}=0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, cost-value coefficient <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, and does
not normalise cost advantages. <span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">IQL-Lagrangian</span> projects the multiplier
to be non-negative and learns independent reward and cost Q-networks with the
IQL-family settings above.
<span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICPO</span> uses independent actor, reward-critic, and cost-critic networks
with hidden widths <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(64,32)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(64,32)</annotation></semantics></math>, cost GAE parameter <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{c}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>c</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{c}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, cost-value
coefficient <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>, target KL <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> conjugate-gradient iterations,
damping <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math>, one Fisher-vector-product sample frequency, and a backtracking
line search with <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>15</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">15</annotation></semantics></math> steps and coefficient <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.8</annotation></semantics></math>. Its cost signal is further
augmented by a learned future-violation predictor: a one-hidden-layer
network of width <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>32</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32</annotation></semantics></math> is trained for <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="25" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>25</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">25</annotation></semantics></math> steps per update to predict whether
a raw safety cost occurs within the next <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>20</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20</annotation></semantics></math> rollout steps, and the predicted
failure probability is added to the raw cost with coefficient <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Shield and contract settings.</h5>

<div id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use discounted-UCB contract selection with discount <math id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.95" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.95</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.95</annotation></semantics></math>, and contract changes only at episode boundaries. Ordinary shielded baselines use the global safety formula for each agent where viable (i.e. apart from <span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RWARE</span>, <span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Connector</span>, and <span id="Pt0.A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Pressure Plate</span>, as previously described in Section <a href="#S6" title="6 Empirical Evaluation ‣ Contract-Based Compositional Shielding for Safe Multi-Agent Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="Pt0.A6.T8" class="ltx_table">
<div id="Pt0.A6.T8.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:90.9pt;vertical-align:-43.8pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-12.0pt,3.2pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<p id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:70%;">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:369.1pt;height:97.3pt;vertical-align:-46.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;">Benchmark</span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;">Max</span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFFFFF;">cand.</span></span></span>
</span></span><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.2.3" class="ltx_text"></span></span>
<span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.2pt 3.0pt;"><span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text"></span> <span id="Pt0.A6.T8.2.1.1.1.1.1.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_text">
